<article class="env-corollary" id="06G6">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06G6">Corollary <span data-tag="06G6">9.3.3.18</span> <span class="named">(Uniqueness)</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \leq \lambda $ be regular cardinals and suppose we are given a commutative diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [dr]_{U} \ar [rr]^{H} &amp;  &amp;  \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \ar [dl]^{ \widehat{U} } \\ &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, &amp;  } \]
</div>
<p> where $U$ and $\widehat{U}$ are inner fibrations and $H$ exhibits $\widehat{U}$ as an $\operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }$-completion of $U$. Let $V: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an inner fibration of simplicial sets which is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-cocomplete, and let $\operatorname{Fun}'_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ be the full subcategory of $\operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ spanned by those objects $F$ such that, for each vertex $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the map of fibers $F_{C}: \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}_{C} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{C}$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary. Then composition with $H$ induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Fun}'_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}). \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Theorem <a data-tag="05L3" href="/tag/05L3">8.7.1.14</a> with Remark <a data-tag="06G4" href="/tag/06G4">9.3.3.16</a> (and Remark <a data-tag="06FD" href="/tag/06FD">9.2.9.8</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
